%% 04a-auth-device-write.mmd - Authentication and authorization: device write path
%% Basis: BRIEF §2, §5 (device authenticates as its installation); WP §9 (401 / 403); LEC S7, S8
%% Decisions: my-decisions §9 (401 vs 403 confirmed by you, OQ-10). Key-hash lookup mechanism is a PROPOSAL.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant D as Device
  participant A as API - authApiKey
  participant DB as MongoDB
  D->>A: POST /solar/v1.0/installations/{installation-id}/readings with X-API-Key
  alt X-API-Key header missing
    A-->>D: 401 + WWW-Authenticate ApiKey realm solar
  else header present
    A->>A: SHA-256 hash of the presented key
    A->>DB: find installation where api_key_hash equals the hash
    alt no installation matches (unknown or invalid key)
      A-->>D: 401 + WWW-Authenticate
    else key belongs to a different installation than the path
      A-->>D: 403 (understood but refused)
    else key belongs to the installation in the path
      A->>A: continue to validation and insert (diagram 05)
    end
  end
  Note over D,A: A JWT sent to this route is not a valid credential, so 401 (PROPOSAL)
  Note over D,A: installation_id is taken from the path only, never from the body
